:name: Two-Node Virtual CAN Network - ECU + Tester
:description: Two independently simulated Nucleo-H753ZI boards, each running real Zephyr firmware, connected over a shared virtual CAN bus inside Renode. Each node's UART is exposed over its own TCP socket so an external process can observe both sides of the CAN exchange independently - the same architecture used to validate ECU-to-tester diagnostic communication on a real CAN bench, just running entirely in simulation.

using sysbus

$bin=@https://dl.antmicro.com/projects/renode/nucleo_h743zi--zephyr-samples-net-sockets-can.elf-s_2243040-d8ba11b258437935c3880cf3e162f448f55c6f17

# Shared virtual CAN bus both nodes will be attached to.
emulation CreateCANHub "canHub"

macro reset
"""
    sysbus LoadELF $bin
"""

################################################
# Node 1 - "ECU"
################################################
mach create "ecu_node"
include @platforms/boards/nucleo_h753zi.repl
runMacro $reset
connector Connect fdcan1 canHub
emulation CreateServerSocketTerminal 3456 "ecuUART"
connector Connect sysbus.usart3 ecuUART

mach clear

################################################
# Node 2 - "Tester"
################################################
mach create "tester_node"
include @platforms/boards/nucleo_h753zi.repl
runMacro $reset
connector Connect fdcan1 canHub
emulation CreateServerSocketTerminal 3457 "testerUART"
connector Connect sysbus.usart3 testerUART

mach clear

start
